Z||000000||prof bobo||11-14-2001||11:14 AM||||I recently bought a new boat and decided to winterize it over the weekend.  It's got the 330 HP Mercury V-8 ('Black Scorpion').  Yeah, there was a moment when I looked at the motor, then looked at my Fiero ...<BR>Anyway, as I was working on it I started looking around the motor to see how familiar things were compared to the Fiero 6.  Maybe I'm missing something, or it's well hidden, but there doesn't seem to be a computer module per se.  I found a box with some electrical components, but only a couple of small modules, perhaps just enough to do spark control and fuel delivery, maybe very application specific.  The point is, how adaptable or useful would this setup be for someone doing a Fiero engine swap?  Seems like it might be ideal for a simple bare bones EFI and I'd suppose it ought to be performance oriented, after all, in my experience marine engines seem to operate in only two modes, idle and wide open.  Opinions?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||11-14-2001||12:03 PM||||boat motor tend to run at steady speeds unlike a car that needs to speed up and slow down much more.cams and spark adv are diffrent as is cooling needs on boats too.<BR>plus boat motors cost more because of marine condisions cause more corosion inside.<BR>someone here found a simple N* controler for a boat motor use, but itis thought too limited/simple to use in a car.<BR>may not pass smog checks, and/or drive smoothly.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pontiaddict||11-15-2001||02:08 AM||||Arizona speed and Marine uses a marine computer that they have reprogramed for automotive use in some of their efi systems. But, unless you purchase a $450 upgrade, it doesn't have closed loop capability.<BR>I don't believe that they sell just the computer either, so you're probably going to have to adapt another type of computer to make the efi work.<BR>If you really want to though, you could contact them and see what they recommend, since they deal with both automotive and marine engines on a daily basis.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.azspeed-marine.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.azspeed-marine.com</A> ||||reg||1
